  "name": "The Gear-Floor of the Ninth Slag Company",
  "scene": "Behind the ice curtain the pump-hall opens out: a dwarf-cut chamber of black iron flywheels tall as cart-wheels, re-toothed with bright new brass by hands that were not Karzum's. Hooded lamps swing on chains, steam hisses along the sluice troughs, and the floor shudders in time with the drainage emptying the town's cistern into Ordokar's galleries. Tally-slates hang from nails beside the pressure governor, chalked over and over with the night's count.",
